{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): mr. hale, vitals real quick. blood pressure's one thirty two over eighty four, and your pulse is seventy six. you're all set.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): hey, come on in, grab a seat. i'm doctor reyes. what's going on with you?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): elbow.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): the elbow, okay. which one, and how's it feeling?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): right. hurts. outside.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): aw, i'm sorry. how long's it been hurting?",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): six weeks.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): what are you up to when it really zings you?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): cup.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): lifting a cup? like your coffee mug?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): yeah.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): the outer bony knob, yeah?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): yeah.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): does the pain run down the arm, or does it stay put?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): stays.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): any numbness or tingling in the fingers?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): swelling, redness, or did you hit it on something?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0020] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): he won't elaborate, he just grinds through the day. oh, his sister takes biotin every morning for her hair, i keep telling him to ask you but.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): ha, that biotin is hers, not a treatment for this. what have you tried for the elbow, and how much?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): ibuprofin. four hundred. twice.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): does the ibuprofen help the pain at all?",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (PATIENT): some.",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): well, actually, um, he skips it half the time. forgets the one after lunch.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): so you're not really getting it twice a day. any other medicine or vitamin?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): allergies to medicines, or anything else?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): tell me about your family, diabetes, blood pressure, whoever you think of.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): uh my father had diabetes in his fifties. mother did not. another sister has pressure but, well, no sugar.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): and your day, the job, the hours, what you eat, exercise, alcohol?",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (PATIENT): i'm a carpenter, ten hour days, i eat whatever's on the truck, no real exercise, couple beers on fridays.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): yeah, that much gripping would do it. let me check. tender right on the outer bump, pain when you extend the wrist against my hand. grip's decent, no swelling.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): err, thinking out loud, all that repetitive grip can irritate the tendon on the outer elbow, and this is most likely tennis elbow. could be a little radial tunnel thing, but i don't think so, and i'm not gonna conclude it's a tear or anything structural yet.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): i'm putting in a referral for physical therapy, and you should wear a forearm brace while you work. no injection today.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): ice it after work, take the ibuprofin with food when you remember, and come back in six weeks."
 ],
